#hasheq((reviewer . "independent read-only reviewer subagents (fresh non-author, reviewer role, model deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash; five rounds over the implementation and its deltas, a new session per round)") (verdict . "APPROVED") (reviewed-sha . "71fc99f3850ebcbf5c9cdf55efdf26c0b9844cc4") (content-digest . "72e39971b879951a0a39b9f3b843272c99e1d274c39745acd38b5c9ed08f9aea") (timestamp . "2026-09-21T23:30:00Z") (scope . "full implementation diff main (69647f1ce5d36798e790b1d62a3b79c62b8b011f) ... content head 71fc99f3850ebcbf5c9cdf55efdf26c0b9844cc4 for v1.00.31 W2 evidence identity and digest integrity (register F2/F3/F4 plus the F12 close-out): scripts/gsd-evidence-bind.rkt (new tool: digest/verify/bind/record-commit with typed verdicts digest-ok/digest-mismatch/malformed-digest/pure/impure-record-commit, the check alias delivering the wave contract's literal --check mode, GIT_*-scrubbed git subprocesses, long-form :(exclude) magic pathspecs byte-identical to the Python digest contract); scripts/gsd-wave-gate.rkt (--receipt-head cross-check emitting head-binding-mismatch naming both SHAs for implementation-sha and reviewed-sha, conditional so historical trios stay readable; sentinel deny-list with typed placeholder-evidence; substantive minimum content on review scope/report and red-first.failure with typed insufficient-review-content; CLI main returns instead of exiting in-process); extensions/gsd/delivery-receipt.rkt (durable-receipt-head accessor); scripts/gsd-delivery.py (prepare() record-commit purity wired to the shared tool, read_staged_trio reviewer-identity assertion); tests/test-gsd-evidence-bind.rkt, tests/test-gsd-wave-gate-digest.rkt, tests/test-gsd-wave-gate.rkt (red-first fixtures with refusal AND control directions; the live W1-range case is shallow-checkout tolerant and skips loudly where history is absent); tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt (falsifiable F2/F3/F4 guards); tests/test-gsd-delivery-receipt.rkt (durable-receipt-head both directions); tests/helpers/w2-mini-git-repo.rkt (hermetic mini git fixture); tests/test-gsd-delivery-controller.py (mixed-commit and sentinel fixtures with truthful second-PR base); tests/test-gsd-governance-workflow.rkt (pass-fixture narratives raised to the minimum-content floors); artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w2/ (matrix with verdict lines extracted verbatim from the raw captures, four red-first captures, SHA256SUMS, retained fast RUN-SUMMARY); README metrics and the canonical tier-ownership matrices regenerated via their generators; docs/reports/EVIDENCE-INTEGRITY-v1.00.31.md (wave report incl. the review-loop and shallow-checkout sections)") (report . "Five rounds. (1) 3c37f443 -> APPROVED with four non-blocking findings; three acted on: the contract's literal --check mode delivered as the check subcommand (fail-closed alias of verify, usage-listed, pinned by a both-directions test), a duplicated require block removed, and the report documents the exit-0 typed-verdict ergonomics note (F8-adjacent) and the binding-time review() reconciliation that accepts a reviewed-sha which is an evidence-only ancestor of the receipt head (what makes pre-merge binding possible; fail-closed via require_receipt_tip on any non-evidence drift). (2) 220f676b -> APPROVED: the delta was exactly the three fixes; round-1 substance re-verified intact. (3) 5a0d0567 delta -> REQUEST_CHANGES, correct: CI's repo lint-quality gate had surfaced two 151-character usage lines and a one-line metric drift that the quick pre-commit lane does not check; both repaired (usage reflowed with identical flags, 7 CLI tests green; metrics resynced), and the reviewer correctly required the trio to be rebound by tooling at the exact head, the test-lines drift named (register fixture format-string reflow), and fresh fast-suite provenance. (4) ae1082ec delta -> REQUEST_CHANGES, correct: the live-checkout W1-range digest case failed in the fast shard because CI clones are depth-1 and the W1 publication commits are absent there (verified by simulating a shallow clone); the case now probes history non-raisingly and skips loudly when absent, and the reviewer required fresh provenance again, honest prose (the old fast detail claimed only artifacts/trio separated the measured head - no longer true), stale-number dedupe, and the caveat recorded rather than hidden. (5) 71fc99f3 (this head, post-rebind) -> APPROVED: the validation record's fast detail is rebuilt as one honest provenance statement for this exact head, the lint numbers match the README at this head (188807/278125/42048), the review record names the final head, the report carries a dedicated shallow-checkout section, and the bound records verify digest-ok at this head with the strict gate passing. Known limitation, stated rather than smoothed: in shallow checkouts the runner reports the live-range file as passed with skip=0 although the live assertion did not execute; CI coverage of the tool contract rests on the synthetic cases, which run everywhere."))
